WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:10.417
FAYE MOSS: Hello, everyone! Faye Moss here with another episode of Superstars in History , where I interview the legends of

2
00:00:10.418 --> 00:00:18.488
the past. In the 1980s and 1990s, today's guest was the most photographed, most famous woman in the

3
00:00:18.489 --> 00:00:28.638
world! She modernized the British royal family with her sense of style, concern for everyone, and efforts to introduce her children to the real world. Please

4
00:00:28.639 --> 00:00:50.941
give a warm welcome to Diana, Princess of Wales! PRINCESS

5
00:00:50.942 --> 00:00:57.538
DIANA: Hello, Faye! I understand your grandmother is sick. How's she doing, and how are you?

6
00:00:57.539 --> 00:01:02.277
FAYE MOSS: She's getting better, thanks. That's so kind of you to

7
00:01:02.278 --> 00:01:06.547
ask. Then again you were known for your kindness, even as a

8
00:01:06.548 --> 00:01:16.419
child. You were born in 1961 and came to public attention later as Lady Diana Spencer. Tell us about your family. PRINCESS

9
00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:21.409
DIANA: The Spencers are one of the oldest, most distinguished families in Great

10
00:01:21.410 --> 00:01:25.259
Britain. The family has been friends with the royal family for generations.

11
00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:31.097
In fact, I grew up on one of the royal family's properties in the countryside. FAYE

12
00:01:31.098 --> 00:01:34.826
MOSS: That must have been a beautiful place to live!

13
00:01:34.827 --> 00:01:39.250
PRINCESS DIANA: It was, but unfortunately my parents' marriage

14
00:01:39.251 --> 00:01:43.851
was troubled. They divorced when I was seven, and that trauma shaped my whole

15
00:01:43.852 --> 00:01:52.051
life. After a bitter legal battle, my father was granted custody of my two older sisters, my younger brother, and me.

16
00:01:52.052 --> 00:01:56.540
FAYE MOSS: Did you feel different from your friends because your parents were

17
00:01:56.541 --> 00:02:02.991
divorced? PRINCESS DIANA: Oh, yes! Hardly anyone got divorced back then. But there was one

18
00:02:02.992 --> 00:02:07.145
positive result: I could always sympathize with people who had

19
00:02:07.146 --> 00:02:14.368
family problems. When I was 13, there was more upheaval because my grandfather died, and my father became Earl

20
00:02:14.369 --> 00:02:19.951
Spencer. We moved two hours away from my friends to live at our family's ancestral home.

21
00:02:19.952 --> 00:02:24.357
Things got worse when my father married someone we all hated! FAYE

22
00:02:24.358 --> 00:02:30.353
MOSS: That's a lot to deal with! Can you tell us some of your happier memories?

23
00:02:30.354 --> 00:02:35.195
PRINCESS DIANA: Loved to swim and dive. Loved tap dancing

24
00:02:35.196 --> 00:02:40.004
and ballet. My dream was to become a ballerina, but I grew too

25
00:02:40.005 --> 00:02:42.923
tall. FAYE MOSS: What did you do

26
00:02:42.924 --> 00:02:48.282
after leaving school? PRINCESS DIANA: I moved to London and worked as an assistant teacher at a nursery

27
00:02:48.283 --> 00:02:52.860
school and a babysitter. I also cleaned house for my oldest sister, Sarah,

28
00:02:52.861 --> 00:02:59.690
and her friends. FAYE MOSS: You were a cleaner before you married a prince? That sounds like something

29
00:02:59.691 --> 00:03:06.149
from a fairy tale! And the Prince of Wales is heir to the British throne, so you'd

30
00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:09.353
eventually be queen! What was it like to date

31
00:03:09.354 --> 00:03:18.207
Prince Charles? PRINCESS DIANA: The British press was always interested in Charles' girlfriends, especially since he was 32, and everyone thought it was time for

32
00:03:18.208 --> 00:03:21.522
him to marry. They went into a frenzy when we

33
00:03:21.523 --> 00:03:28.689
started dating. Every day dozens of reporters and photographers waited outside my flat and chased

34
00:03:28.690 --> 00:03:35.685
my car. FAYE MOSS: The tabloids called you "Shy Di" because you ducked your head whenever they tried

35
00:03:35.686 --> 00:03:40.959
to photograph you. You were so young and pretty, and everyone loved that you

36
00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:48.497
were shy! PRINCESS DIANA: I wasn't shy—I was terrified! I was only 19, but the paparazzi wouldn't

37
00:03:48.498 --> 00:03:54.645
leave me alone. I had no choice but to cope if I wanted the prince to marry me—and I wanted that

38
00:03:54.646 --> 00:03:58.621
very much. As king, Charles would be the head of the Church of

39
00:03:58.622 --> 00:04:07.301
England. I naively thought this meant he couldn't get divorced, so my children would never suffer as I had. We'd live happily ever after.

40
00:04:07.302 --> 00:04:15.208
FAYE MOSS: More than 750 million people around the world watched your fairy-tale wedding on TV in

41
00:04:15.209 --> 00:04:18.748
1981. Did you hope the press would stop hounding you after that?

42
00:04:18.749 --> 00:04:24.161
PRINCESS DIANA: Of course! But the wedding only increased interest in everything about

43
00:04:24.162 --> 00:04:36.087
me. FAYE MOSS: Well, you were very stylish. The rest of the royal family looked rather . . . um . . . old-fashioned, but you were a British

44
00:04:36.088 --> 00:04:40.197
fashion icon. PRINCESS DIANA: Yes, but I wanted to be known for more

45
00:04:40.198 --> 00:04:45.819
than my clothes. Charles, as heir, had a clearly defined role, but there wasn't one

46
00:04:45.820 --> 00:04:54.976
for me. On our official visits, I gradually realized that I could help people—the sick, the dying, the abused—just by being

47
00:04:54.977 --> 00:04:59.978
there. People were starving for love, and that was something I could give.

48
00:04:59.979 --> 00:05:08.052
FAYE MOSS: Right. Before you, the royal family was a lot more distant from people, and many people credit you for updating its

49
00:05:08.053 --> 00:05:16.888
image. PRINCESS DIANA: I believed the monarchy needed to be relevant to modern people's lives, so I became involved in causes that the royal family had mostly

50
00:05:16.889 --> 00:05:22.545
avoided. I was honored to be asked to open the first British hospital ward for HIV/AIDS patients.

51
00:05:22.546 --> 00:05:30.719
There was such a huge stigma attached to the disease then that I made international headlines just by shaking hands with a patient. FAYE

52
00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:38.552
MOSS: You made a big impact, and your fame helped you do it. But being in the spotlight wasn't easy for you.

53
00:05:38.553 --> 00:05:44.095
PRINCESS DIANA: Sadly my marriage wasn't very happy since my husband was in love with someone

54
00:05:44.096 --> 00:05:52.131
else. I grew depressed and struggled with an eating disorder, which went on for years until a friend persuaded me to seek help.

55
00:05:52.132 --> 00:05:58.874
My own experiences gave me great compassion for those with mental illness. FAYE

56
00:05:58.875 --> 00:06:03.041
MOSS: I can't believe we haven't talked about your children yet!

57
00:06:03.042 --> 00:06:05.611
They were so important to you.

58
00:06:05.612 --> 00:06:11.201
PRINCESS DIANA: My boys! William was born in 1982 and Harry, two years

59
00:06:11.202 --> 00:06:14.434
later. I wanted them to lead normal lives, if

60
00:06:14.435 --> 00:06:22.553
possible. Unlike my husband, they attended school with other children right from the start, and we went to movies and amusement parks. FAYE

61
00:06:22.554 --> 00:06:27.167
MOSS: You took them to hospitals, hospices, and homeless

62
00:06:27.168 --> 00:06:30.579
shelters. Was that decision influenced by your own work?

63
00:06:30.580 --> 00:06:37.881
PRINCESS DIANA: Yes, it was especially important for William to see how real people live since he was in the line of

64
00:06:37.882 --> 00:06:49.746
succession. As for me, I eventually grew tired of the glamorous parts of being Princess of Wales and focused on my charitable work. I had no desire to be queen. FAYE

65
00:06:49.747 --> 00:06:57.016
MOSS: Thank you for this refreshingly candid interview. We'll let you get back to history

66
00:06:57.017 --> 00:07:02.939
now. PRINCESS DIANA: Thank

67
00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:13.620
you, Faye! FAYE MOSS: Princess Diana's marriage ended in divorce in 1996, but she stayed in the public eye, raising awareness of the problem

68
00:07:13.621 --> 00:07:21.018
of land mines. The next year she died in a car accident that occurred while her driver was trying to elude

69
00:07:21.019 --> 00:07:29.301
the paparazzi. The world went into mourning, and huge crowds lined London's streets for her funeral while millions watched on

70
00:07:29.302 --> 00:07:37.159
TV. Now adults with families of their own, Diana's sons continue her legacy of caring and concern for others.

71
00:07:37.160 --> 00:07:49.317
That's all for now on Superstars in History . I'm Faye Moss.

